<title>SOUTH KOREA: Shindongbang buys 50,000T U.S. soybean.</title>
<headline>Shindongbang buys 50,000T U.S. soybean.</headline>
<dateline>SEOUL 1996-11-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>South Korea's Shindongbang Corp bought 50,000 tonnes of U.S. No.2 soybean at basis price over November futures on the Chicago Board of Trade, a senior official of the company said on Monday.</p>
<p>The official said shipment was set for the first half of November from the U.S. Gulf. Arrival was slated for December 20 to the western port city of Inchon.</p>
<p>He said the purchasing price was around $305 per tonne, C&amp;F, from an unnamed U.S. grain exporter.</p>
<p>--Seoul Newsroom (822) 727 5651</p>
</text>
